<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mughal Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mughals, Mughal dynasty, Mughal</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mughal Empire was a dynasty of Timurid descent that ruled much of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-subcontinent">Indian subcontinent</a> from 1526, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babur">Babur</a> defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lodi-dynasty">Lodi</a> sultan at Panipat. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akbar">Akbar</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jahangir">Jahangir</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-jahan">Shah Jahan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aurangzeb">Aurangzeb</a> it became one of the richest states in the world. It was weakened by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> wars and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a>'s invasion of 1739, and ended under British rule in 1857.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mughal-empire.jpg" alt="Mughal Empire" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TRAJAN 117 This bitmap image was created with Windows Paint. · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mughal_Empire_(1700).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
